@startuml Sequence Diagram - User Authentication and Spell Retrieval
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam FontColor #000000

title Sequence Diagram - User Authentication and Spell Retrieval Flow

actor User
participant "Browser\n(React App)" as Browser
participant "Web Service\n(NGINX)" as WebService
participant "API Gateway\n(Express)" as Gateway
participant "Auth Service\n(Express)" as AuthService
participant "Spell Service\n(Express)" as SpellService
database "MySQL\nDatabases" as Database

== User Registration ==
User -> Browser: 1. Enter credentials\n(username, email, password)
Browser -> WebService: 2. POST /api/auth/register\n(form data)
WebService -> Gateway: 3. Forward to API Gateway
Gateway -> AuthService: 4. POST /api/auth/register
AuthService -> Database: 5. Query: Check if user exists\nSELECT * FROM users\nWHERE email=? OR username=?
Database --> AuthService: 6. No existing user (success)
AuthService -> AuthService: 7. Hash password\n(bcrypt.hash)
AuthService -> Database: 8. INSERT INTO users\n(username, email, password_hash)
Database --> AuthService: 9. User created\n(insertId returned)
AuthService --> Gateway: 10. 201 Created\n{userId: 123}
Gateway --> WebService: 11. Response forwarded
WebService --> Browser: 12. Success response
Browser -> User: 13. Show success message

== User Login ==
User -> Browser: 14. Enter login credentials\n(email, password)
Browser -> WebService: 15. POST /api/auth/login\n(email, password)
WebService -> Gateway: 16. Forward request
Gateway -> AuthService: 17. POST /api/auth/login
AuthService -> Database: 18. SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE email=?
Database --> AuthService: 19. User found with password_hash
AuthService -> AuthService: 20. Verify password\n(bcrypt.compare)
AuthService -> AuthService: 21. Generate JWT Token\n(jwt.sign)
AuthService --> Gateway: 22. 200 OK\n{token: "eyJ..."}
Gateway --> WebService: 23. Response with token
WebService --> Browser: 24. Send token to frontend
Browser -> Browser: 25. Store token\n(localStorage/sessionStorage)

== Fetch Spells (with optional auth) ==
User -> Browser: 26. Navigate to /spells
Browser -> Browser: 27. Read token from storage
Browser -> WebService: 28. GET /api/spells\n(Authorization header with token)
WebService -> Gateway: 29. Forward request with token
Gateway -> Gateway: 30. Verify JWT Token\n(optional auth middleware)
Gateway -> SpellService: 31. GET /api/spells\n(with user context if authenticated)
SpellService -> Database: 32. SELECT * FROM spells\n(+ JOIN with user_id if needed)
Database --> SpellService: 33. Return spell list\n[{id, name, traditions...}]
SpellService --> Gateway: 34. 200 OK\n{spells: [...]}
Gateway --> WebService: 35. Response forwarded
WebService --> Browser: 36. Send spell data
Browser -> Browser: 37. Parse JSON response\n(setSpells state)
Browser -> User: 38. Display SpellList component\nwith all spells

== Create New Spell (Authenticated) ==
User -> Browser: 39. Submit new spell form
Browser -> Browser: 40. Read JWT token
Browser -> WebService: 41. POST /api/spells\n(spell data + token)
WebService -> Gateway: 42. Forward with Authorization header
Gateway -> Gateway: 43. Verify JWT Token\n(required auth middleware)
Gateway -> SpellService: 44. POST /api/spells\n(spell data + user_id from token)
SpellService -> Database: 45. INSERT INTO spells\n(name, traditions, components...)\nINSERT INTO spellbooks\n(user_id, spell_id)
Database --> SpellService: 46. Spell created\n(insertId)
SpellService --> Gateway: 47. 201 Created\n{spell: {...}}
Gateway --> WebService: 48. Response forwarded
WebService --> Browser: 49. Success response
Browser -> Browser: 50. Update spells state\n(addSpell)
Browser -> User: 51. Show new spell in list

@enduml